>Synopsis:	textproc/libxml2: update to 2.15.3
>Severity:	serious
>Priority:	medium
>Category:	pkg
>Class:		change-request
>Release:	NetBSD 11.0, pkgsrc trunk fa7ad771c96929bf742033e6ccfd8bb45b9cab49
>Environment:
System: NetBSD 11.0 i386
Architecture: i386
Machine: i386
>Description:
	pkgsrc has libxml2 2.15.1 (textproc/libxml2/Makefile.common rev 1.31,
	2026-02-19).  Upstream released 2.15.2 on 2026-03-03 and 2.15.3 on
	2026-04-15.

	2.15.2 fixes five issues that pkg-vulnerabilities currently lists
	against every version of the package:

	  CVE-2025-8732   uncontrolled recursion in xmlParseSGMLCatalog
	                  (NEWS: "catalog: fix stack overflow from
	                  self-referencing SGML CATALOG entries")
	  CVE-2026-0989   RelaxNG include limit added
	  CVE-2026-0990   infinite recursion in xmlCatalogListXMLResolve
	  CVE-2026-0992   exponential behaviour in entity handling
	  CVE-2026-1757   memory leak in the xmllint shell

	2.15.3 adds a type confusion fix in xmlParseReference and in
	xmlC14NProcessAttrsAxis, a double free in the Python bindings, and
	several memory leak fixes.

	For background on why the package sat still: upstream declared libxml2
	unmaintained in September 2025 and the GitLab page still says so, but
	releases resumed.  2.15.2 and 2.15.3 were made by a different set of
	contributors.

	The remaining pkg-vulnerabilities entry for this package,
	CVE-2025-12863, is not named in the 2.15.2 or 2.15.3 NEWS, so I do not
	know whether it is fixed and I am not asking for that entry to change.

	Five pkg-vulnerabilities entries should be narrowed at the same time as
	this update.  They currently read

	  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	.../CVE-2025-8732
	  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	.../CVE-2026-0989
	  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	.../CVE-2026-0990
	  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	.../CVE-2026-0992
	  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	.../CVE-2026-1757

	and all five are named as fixed in the 2.15.2 NEWS, so they can become

	  libxml2<2.15.2	...

	Without that, updating the package does not stop pkg_admin audit from
	reporting them, because the entries match every version.

>How-To-Repeat:
	cd /usr/pkgsrc/textproc/libxml2 && make show-var VARNAME=DISTNAME
	  -> libxml2-2.15.1

	pkg_admin audit reports the five CVEs above against any installed
	libxml2, because the pkg-vulnerabilities entries are written as
	libxml2-[0-9]* (every version).

>Fix:
	The one patch pkgsrc carries for this package, patch-configure, still
	applies unchanged against 2.15.3.  distinfo regenerated.

	textproc/py-libxml2 shares Makefile.common and is updated by the same
	change.

	Built and packaged on NetBSD 11.0/i386.

	Please also narrow the five pkg-vulnerabilities entries listed above to
	libxml2<2.15.2 when this goes in; the update alone does not clear
	pkg_admin audit.

	Index: textproc/libxml2/Makefile.common
